  "request": "Jack, 10 November 2026 (native thread), following Pedro's 6 Nov meeting ('we need to make them more image kind of'; 'the words are good but we need to accompany that with some proof'; go back to the image-led original but improved): do not cut any words; make the site feel image-led; add images wherever there are cards (number 1 priority) and wherever long text sections lack images. Images supplement the cards and copy. Private evidence: hqc-20261106-actions/imagegen-nov10 and the meeting transcript in Jack's vault.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "M0",
      "text": "Planning amendment for the image-led round (10 Nov); all earlier requirements, including the 9 Nov illustrative-label removal, stay in force (cumulative acceptance matrix)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "text": "OutcomePage cards: every outcome card (3) and every scope card (including 'Confirmed before work') gets an image from the new card library, relevant to the card text; every related-route card shows the destination page's existing hero image. No image repeats within one page. Exception: the reviews-case-studies outcome and scope cards stay text-only because they sit beside evidence wording."
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "text": "Homepage: the five service-process cards ('Clarity before anyone picks up a cloth') and the six complex-process step cards each get a distinct relevant image."
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "text": "Contact page information cards (Existing Clients, Suppliers and Subcontractors, Media/Partnerships, Assessment Media, Service Area Questions, Need a Cleaning Quote) and the four request-a-quote route cards each get an image; the quote route cards reuse the existing three-offerings images."
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "text": "OutcomePage long copy sections: controlled-copy sections that currently have no imagery get one supporting image laid out beside or above the text (alternating on desktop, stacked on mobile), so pages read image-led; existing section imagery stays where it is. No image repeats within one page. reviews-case-studies sections and any section whose copy is evidence, proof, review or client-count wording get no generated image."
    },
    {
      "id": "G1",
      "text": "Add the generated card-library images under public/images/phase8-nov10/ (Codex ImageGen, house style, deep-teal plain uniforms, no text, logos or identifiable faces), with factual alt text. Generated images are never labelled or described as HQC work."
    },
    {
      "id": "R3",
      "text": "Record the resulting version in the review room (append; note: image-led cards and sections, no copy change) and in revisions/versions.json; full npm run check:revision passes."
    }
  ],
